{%- doc -%}
Renders a "Buy via WhatsApp" button for the product page. Reuses the shared button component
(snippets/button.liquid) for its design (border-radius, font, sizing, animations) — only the colors are
independent from the rest of the theme's buttons.

@param {object} [product] - the product to build the prefilled message/link for
@param {string} [phone_number] - WhatsApp phone number, international format, no symbols
@param {string} [message] - base message text (the product name and link are appended automatically)
@param {string} [button_text] - visible button label
@param {string} [button_style] - "solid" or "link"
@param {object} [background_color] - color setting object
@param {object} [text_color] - color setting object
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  # One source of truth: the "Atención por WhatsApp" section of the overlay group (sections/vc-whatsapp-button.liquid)
  # - the same main number for everyone, and this button's text, style, colors and fallback message. Its section id
  # is the key the overlay group stores it under (sections/overlay-group.json). If that section isn't there (deleted
  # or re-added with another id), the block falls back to its own settings, so the button never disappears.
  assign advisor = sections['vc_whatsapp_button_YAUfVC']
  assign hide_button = false

  if advisor != blank and advisor.settings.show_product_button == false
    assign hide_button = true
  elsif advisor != blank
    assign phone_number = advisor.settings.phone_number | default: phone_number
    assign message = advisor.settings.product_message | default: message
    assign button_text = advisor.settings.product_button_text | default: button_text
    assign button_style = advisor.settings.product_button_style | default: button_style

    if advisor.settings.product_button_bg != blank
      assign background_color = advisor.settings.product_button_bg
    endif

    if advisor.settings.product_button_text_color != blank
      assign text_color = advisor.settings.product_button_text_color
    endif
  endif

  assign wa_text = message
  if product != blank
    assign wa_text = wa_text | append: ' ' | append: product.title | append: ' - ' | append: request.origin | append: product.url
  endif
  assign wa_encoded_text = wa_text | url_encode
  # wa.me only accepts digits: tolerate a "+", spaces or dashes typed in the setting
  assign wa_phone = phone_number | remove: '+' | remove: ' ' | remove: '-'
  assign wa_href = 'https://wa.me/' | append: wa_phone | append: '?text=' | append: wa_encoded_text

  # Label with its last word underlined (trailing punctuation stays outside the underline)
  assign label_safe = button_text | escape
  assign label_words = label_safe | split: ' '
  assign label_last = label_words | last
  assign label_core = label_last | remove: '.' | remove: ',' | remove: '!' | remove: '?' | remove: ':'
  assign label_tail = label_last | remove: label_core
  assign label_head = label_safe | replace_last: label_last, ''
-%}

{%- comment -%}Markup written out as a template (not built by string appends) so it is output as real HTML, never as visible text{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture button_text_html -%}{{ label_head }}<span class="whatsapp-buy-button__last">{{ label_core }}</span>{{ label_tail }}{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%} Without a number the link would be a dead wa.me/?text=..., so nothing is rendered until the block is filled in {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if hide_button == false and wa_phone != blank and button_text != blank -%}
{%- if button_style == 'link' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
  Same "plain text link" positioning as the product description's show-more/less toggle
  (snippets/product-info.liquid), but without .link's own underline (background gradient, theme.css):
  a permanent underline under a secondary action like this read as visual noise/competed with the
  WhatsApp icon-less text for attention - color alone (faded, same as that toggle) is enough to mark
  it as secondary. Still skips snippets/button.liquid, whose own style: 'link' adds .subheading (its
  own font scale) and the WhatsApp icon, neither of which is wanted here.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <style>
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .whatsapp-buy-button--link {
      color: rgb(var(--text-color) / .5);
      background: none;
    }
  </style>

  <a href="{{ wa_href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link whatsapp-buy-button whatsapp-buy-button--link">
    {{- label_head -}}<span class="whatsapp-buy-button__last">{{- label_core -}}</span>{{- label_tail -}}
  </a>
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%}
  size: 'sm' (snippets/button.liquid's own "sm" size, not a new style) keeps this visually secondary
  to the Add to cart button above it (buy-buttons.liquid, always full-size + stretch: true) - without
  it, WhatsApp's bold brand green at full size could outweigh the primary action instead of
  supporting it, especially against an Add to cart button configured with a muted/outline-like
  background (eg. this theme's current white background + dark border default).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'button',
      content: button_text_html,
      href: wa_href,
      external: true,
      icon: 'whatsapp',
      style: button_style,
      size: 'sm',
      background: background_color,
      text_color: text_color,
      class: 'whatsapp-buy-button'
  -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
This button acts like the floating WhatsApp button: clicking it opens that button's list of agents so the customer
can choose, instead of going straight to one chat. That behavior lives in ONE place - the script of
sections/vc-whatsapp-button.liquid, which listens for clicks on ".whatsapp-buy-button" - so this snippet is only
markup. Without JS, without a visible floating button or without agents there is nothing to open, so the link keeps
working as a plain wa.me link (the number and message of this block).
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .whatsapp-buy-button__last {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: .2em;
  }
</style>
